@startuml UC005_Feed_Scroll_Sequence
!theme plain
title UC005 — Public feed and incremental React cards
actor "Visitor / signed-in user" as Viewer
participant "public/js/app.js" as Shell
participant "frontend/feed/mountFeed.jsx" as Mount
participant "frontend/feed/FeedPage.jsx\n+ useFeed.js" as Feed
participant "frontend/feed/feedApi.js" as Client
participant "src/routes/feed.routes.js" as Routes
participant "src/services/feedService.js" as Service
participant "src/db/database.js" as Data
database PostgreSQL as DB

Viewer -> Shell : Enter website / #/feed
Shell -> Mount : Mount one React feed root with shared transport
Mount -> Feed : Render FeedPage
Feed -> Client : Load first page (limit 10)
Client -> Routes : GET /api/feed?limit=10 (public)
Routes -> Service : Read published feed; optional viewer identity
Service -> Data : Fetch ordered page and counts
Data -> DB : Published posts ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC\nLIMIT 11; page-scoped counts
DB --> Data : Page boundary and result rows
Data --> Service : Post summaries and has-next information
Service --> Routes : Public projection and opaque nextCursor
Routes --> Client : 200 { posts, nextCursor }
Client --> Feed : First batch
Feed -> Feed : Create ProjectPost components for fetched IDs only
Feed --> Viewer : Show cards; lazy media and collapsed comments

loop Sentinel near viewport / Load more, while nextCursor exists
  Viewer -> Feed : Scroll toward the bottom / activate Load more
  Feed -> Feed : Guard one in-flight request; retain cursor
  Feed -> Client : Request next batch
  Client -> Routes : GET /api/feed?cursor=...&limit=10
  Routes -> Service : Read next published page
  Service -> Data : Keyset read older than cursor boundary
  Data -> DB : Read next bounded page and counts
  DB --> Data : Rows and next-page information
  Data --> Service : Page data
  Service --> Routes : Public projection and nextCursor
  Routes --> Client : 200 page / error response
  Client --> Feed : posts and nextCursor
  Feed -> Feed : Deduplicate IDs, append cards, advance cursor
  Feed --> Viewer : Additional cards; stop if cursor is null

end
Viewer -> Shell : Leave feed route
Shell -> Mount : Unmount feed before replacing DOM
Mount -> Feed : Abort reads; disconnect observer; ignore stale results
note over Feed, DB
  Scrolling creates React components, never database posts.
  Comments load separately only when opened.
  End of published projects is a finite end-of-feed state.
end note
@enduml
